Changes: zero-based indexing, half-open blocks, arbitrary finite positive
seeds, generalized predicates and proofs, and a single odd-exponent power
square-gap argument replacing the two-power plateau argument. The source
file's fixed-seed quantitative theorems are not included or claimed here.

That upstream file credits Google DeepMind's Formal Conjectures project
(Copyright 2026 The Formal Conjectures Authors; Apache License 2.0) for its
original problem definitions. This package uses different generalized
definitions; the relationship and index shift are documented in STATEMENT.md.

